    "answer": {
      "short": "The maximum area is $11\\,250\\text{ m}^2$, attained with sides $75\\text{ m}$ perpendicular to the fence and length $150\\text{ m}$ along it. Restrictions are $0<x<150$, $0<300-2x<300$ and $A>0$.",
      "worked": "Let the perpendicular side length be $x$ metres and the remaining fenced side length be $L$ metres.\n$$\\begin{align*}2x+L&=300\\\\L&=300-2x\\\\A(x)&=x(300-2x)\\\\A(x)&=-2x^2+300x\\\\A(x)&=-2(x-75)^2+11\\,250.\\end{align*}$$\nSince $(x-75)^2\\geq0$, the maximum area is $11\\,250\\text{ m}^2$ when $x=75\\text{ m}$. Then $L=300-2(75)=150\\text{ m}$.\nBoth dimensions must be positive, giving $0<x<150$ and $0<L<300$. The area satisfies $0<A\\leq11\\,250$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
